  "limitations": [
    "The admitted Work retains the minimized validated execution envelope alongside a separate schema-derived redacted operator projection, as required by plans 04 and 13. Secret-classified material is rejected; SAFE-07 owns later retention-time pseudonymization and deletion.",
    "The catalog and planner seal the output schema content hash, and a registered adapter must reproduce it before the call. Provider name, version, mode, and observation identity remain adapter assertions; RUN-06 persists them but does not introduce live provider attestation.",
    "The controlled READ completion seam currently creates artifacts with Work and external-observation sources and no parent artifact IDs. The repository enforces exact same-Run ancestor lineage when parents are supplied, but dependency-output binding into execution remains ORCH-05 and workflow-composition scope.",
    "Tests use deterministic adapters, injected clocks, and trusted file-backed SQLite. They do not execute live model or connector providers, a distributed worker fleet, or hostile database administration.",
    "PostgreSQL DDL portability is checked for artifact constraints, but PostgreSQL runtime locking and transaction behavior are not executed. DEL-04 owns Alembic revisions, upgrade and downgrade verification, and deployed-schema rollout.",
    "The durable timeline is an application and repository contract. API-07 and WEB-06 retain public run, artifact, and audit projections, filtering, pagination protocol, and the operator timeline UI."
  ]
